            {
                "entry_id": "f75c64c9-0b38-36c6-b9bc-6dc5bba5c60e",
                "word": "childing",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "26aa85f2-306e-3cd1-96c3-4171b8516eb1",
                        "entry_id": "f75c64c9-0b38-36c6-b9bc-6dc5bba5c60e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "gerund of child: the act or process of childbearing or childbirth."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic",
                            "form-of",
                            "gerund",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "46d788eb-6637-4082-a6ee-c26cb82ea000",
                                "sense_id": "26aa85f2-306e-3cd1-96c3-4171b8516eb1",
                                "text": "This Conſtantia was fiftie yeares of age before ſhe was conceiued with him; whom the emperor Henrie the ſixth to auoide all doubt and ſurmiſe that of hir conception and childing might be thought, and to the perill of the empire inſue: cauſed his regall tent to be pitched abrode in place where euery man might reſort."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9e67caf6-2549-4926-9cd1-8e1e6f398281",
                                "sense_id": "26aa85f2-306e-3cd1-96c3-4171b8516eb1",
                                "text": "When Zalzer is grown up, and leaves the nest, the Simorg gives him one of her feathers, telling him, whenever he is in great distress, to burn it, and she will immediately come to his assistance. Zalzer marries Rodahver, who is likely to die in childing; he then burns the feather, and the Simorg appears and orders the Cæsarean operation to be performed."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6f8494db-a0f9-499c-916b-c44f0a4f2bba",
                                "sense_id": "26aa85f2-306e-3cd1-96c3-4171b8516eb1",
                                "text": "[H]e had grown up there and there wedded a wife; but that when she died in childing with her first bairn, and the bairn had not lived, he loathed the place, and came back again into the Dale."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "13d30d35-cd8a-4bf0-a45a-08ff179807d8",
                                "sense_id": "26aa85f2-306e-3cd1-96c3-4171b8516eb1",
                                "text": "I only wish you had arrived this day past. For we had a feast in honor of my wife's childing and her father's visit. Your arrival would have given us even more to be glad for."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
